The orchestrator builds the prior path-to-OID map and the base worktree rows once from the base generation's members and hands them to Pass 2 (index_file) and Pass 3 (worktree), which resolve every path through in-memory HashMap lookups instead of per-file SQL point queries in the hot loop. Both passes therefore depend on the maps being complete for their own source before they are entered — a pass that starts consulting the store directly, or an orchestrator that narrows what it seeds, reintroduces the per-file query cost with no signature or test change to reveal it.
